            "start": [
                [
                    "^I thought it was over. I went back to the boats. I went back to the only thing I knew how to do when I wasn't failing Him. But the nets were empty until He spoke.",
                    {
                        "*": "questions",
                        "flg": 2,
                        "s": [
                            "^What did He ask you?"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "*": "fish",
                        "flg": 2,
                        "s": [
                            "^The catch was miraculous?"
                        ]
                    },
                    null
                ],
                null
            ],
            "fish": [
                [
                    "^One hundred and fifty-three. I counted them myself. The net should have broken, but it held. Just like His grace held when I expected it to snap.",
                    {
                        "*": "questions",
                        "flg": 2,
                        "s": [
                            "^What happened on the shore?"
                        ]
                    },
                    null
                ],
                null
            ],
            "questions": [
                [
                    "^Three times he asked me. One for every time I said 'I do not know him.' He didn't ask for an apology. He asked for my heart. 'Do you love me?'",
                    {
                        "*": "feeding",
                        "flg": 2,
                        "s": [
                            "^And your answer?"
                        ]
                    },
                    null
                ],
                null
            ],
            "feeding": [
                [
                    "^I told Him He knows all things. He knows I love Him, even in my weakness. He told me to feed His sheep. He's trusting me again.",
